  "description": "The French Restoration style was predominantly Neoclassicism, though it also showed the beginnings of Romanticism in music and literature. The term describes the arts, architecture, and decorative arts of the Bourbon Restoration period (1814–1830), during the reign of Louis XVIII and Charles X  from the fall of Napoleon to the July Revolution of 1830 and the beginning of the reign of Louis-Philippe.",
